            <meta charset=3D"UTF-8">
            <title>County waives tipping fees</title>
        </head>

        <body style=3D"font-family: Helvetica, Arial; line-height:1.5">
        <!-- Header start-->
        <div>
            <div><p class=3D"p1" style=3D"text-align: center;"><span style=
=3D"color: #7e8c8d;"><em>This is an urgent message from the County of Kaua'=
i through Everbridge, the County's mass notification system.</em></span></p=
>
            </div>
            <!-- Header end-->
            <!-- Messages start-->
            <div  style=3D"margin-top:30px;" >
                <p> Sept. 9, 6:05 p.m. UPDATE =E2=80=93 County of Kaua=CA=
=BBi Solid Waste Division<br><br>L=C4=AAHU=CA=BBE =E2=80=93 The County of K=
aua=CA=BBi Solid Waste Division is waiving tipping fees for storm-generated=
 debris at the Kekaha Landfill and Refuse Transfer Stations as residents an=
d businesses clean up following Hurricane Lowell.<br><br>=E2=80=9COur famil=
ies are hauling out water-damaged furniture, spoiled food, and whole trees =
from their yards, and the last thing we want is a fee standing between them=
 and getting their homes back in order,=E2=80=9D said Mayor Derek S.K. Kawa=
kami. =E2=80=9CWaiving these fees is one way we can lighten the load. Pleas=
e be patient with our crews at the landfill and transfer stations. They are=
 working long hours to keep these facilities open for you.=E2=80=9D<br><br>=
There is no charge for storm-generated debris, including commercial loads.<=
br><br>**Facility status:**<br><br>* Kekaha Landfill and Hanap=C4=93p=C4=93=
 Refuse Transfer Station are open.<br>* Hanalei, L=C4=ABhu=CA=BBe and Kapa=
=CA=BBa Refuse Transfer Stations are closed due to access issues and will r=
eopen when trailers can be hauled to the landfill.<br>* Green waste is bein=
g accepted at L=C4=ABhu=CA=BBe and Kapa=CA=BBa until capacity is reached. P=
lease keep green waste free of trash, dirt and construction debris.<br>* Re=
fuse collection remains suspended due to downed and low-hanging wires. Plea=
se leave carts out and accessible.<br>* The County=E2=80=99s recycling cont=
ractor remains without power and cannot service Kaua=CA=BBi Recycles bins o=
r process HI-5 materials. Service will resume once power is restored.<br><b=
r>Landfill hours are 8 a.m. to 4 p.m. for residential loads and 8 a.m. to 3=
:30 p.m. for commercial loads. The landfill is closed from noon to 12:30 p.=
m.<br><br>Residents are asked to separate waste into green waste, metals, p=
utrescible waste and dry waste. Please prioritize putrescible waste, such a=
s food, to reduce odors and pests while collection services are disrupted. =
Keep mixed waste free of rainwater and other liquids, including cooking oil=
.<br><br>To sign up for Everbridge emergency notifications, text =E2=80=9CK=
AUAIEMA=E2=80=9D to 888777 or call KEMA at 808-241-1800.<br><br>###<br><br>
<br>Message Sender: Alden  Alayvilla  =20
<br>Notification Status: New  =20
<br>Tipping fees waived for storm debris at Kekaha Landfill and refuse tran=
sfer stations as Kauai cleans up after Hurricane Lowell.</p>
